research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-convergent-implies-absolutely-convergent.prompt.md-999-- **Why the distinction earns a page.** Every result on this page separates the
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-convergent-implies-absolutely-convergent.prompt.md-1000-  two classes. An absolutely convergent series may be reordered at will
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-convergent-implies-absolutely-convergent.prompt.md-1001-  ([[thm-dirichlet-rearrangement]]) and multiplied by another
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-convergent-implies-absolutely-convergent.prompt.md:1002:  ([[thm-mertens]]); a conditionally convergent one may be reordered to any sum
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-convergent-implies-absolutely-convergent.prompt.md-1003-  whatever ([[thm-riemann-series-theorem]]). The difference is not one of degree.
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-convergent-implies-absolutely-convergent.prompt.md-1004-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-convergent-implies-absolutely-convergent.prompt.md-1005-- **A series of nonnegative terms converges absolutely if it converges at all**,
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-convergent-implies-absolutely-convergent.prompt.md-1006-  since then $|a_k| = a_k$. So the distinction is invisible for the comparison,
--
