research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-663-## Facts & Assumptions
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-664-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-665-**Given:** Sequences $(a_k)$ and $(b_k)$ with $\sum |a_k|$ and $\sum |b_k|$ convergent, sums $L_a$ and $L_b$ respectively, partial sums $P_N = \sum_{k<N}|a_k|$ and $Q_m = \sum_{j<m}|b_j|$, and the Cauchy product $c_n = \sum_{k=0}^{n} a_k b_{n-k}$ ([[def-cauchy-product]]).
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-666-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md:667:[L1] The finite identity of [[thm-mertens]], claim 1: for arbitrary sequences $(x_k)$, $(y_k)$ with partial sums $Y_m = \sum_{j<m} y_j$ and Cauchy product $(z_n)$, one has $\sum_{n<N} z_n = \sum_{i<N} x_i\, Y_{N-i}$ for every $N$.
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-668-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md:669:[L2] Mertens' theorem, claim 2 of [[thm-mertens]]: if $\sum x_k$ converges absolutely and $\sum y_k$ converges, their Cauchy product converges to the product of the sums.
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-670-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-671-[L3] $\bigl|\sum_{k<n} x_k\bigr| \le \sum_{k<n}|x_k|$ ([[lem-triangle-inequality-finite]]).
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-672-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-673-[L4] Absolute value: $|xy| = |x|\,|y|$ and $|x| \ge 0$ ([[lem-of-abs-value]]).
--
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-701-6.1 The hypotheses of Mertens' theorem hold, $\sum a_k$ converging absolutely and $\sum b_k$ converging by step 1.1 and [L8]; so $\sum c_n$ converges with sum $AB$. [given, L2, L8] ∎
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-702-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-703-## Remarks
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-704-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md:705:- **Only claim 1 of [[thm-mertens]] is reused, and it is reused for a different pair of sequences.** The identity there is proved for arbitrary real sequences and carries no convergence hypothesis, which is exactly what allows it to be applied here to $(|a_k|)$ and $(|b_k|)$. Nothing about the absolute values is reproved.
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-706-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-707-- **The bound is not an equality.** The sum of $\sum|c_n|$ can be strictly less than $L_a L_b$, since cancellation inside each $c_n$ is invisible to $\gamma_n$; the inequality is all that is claimed and all that is needed.
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-708-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-709-- **Absolute convergence of both factors is a genuine strengthening.** Mertens' theorem already gives $\sum c_n = AB$ with only one factor absolutely convergent; what the second hypothesis buys is that the product series is itself absolutely convergent, hence unconditionally convergent ([[thm-dirichlet-rearrangement]]), so that its terms may be reordered in turn.
--
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-794-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-795-- **Why the distinction earns a page.** Every result on this page separates the
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-796-  two classes. An absolutely convergent series may be reordered at will
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-797-  ([[thm-dirichlet-rearrangement]]) and multiplied by another
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md:798:  ([[thm-mertens]]); a conditionally convergent one may be reordered to any sum
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-799-  whatever ([[thm-riemann-series-theorem]]). The difference is not one of degree.
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-800-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-801-- **A series of nonnegative terms converges absolutely if it converges at all**,
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-mertens.md-802-  since then $|a_k| = a_k$. So the distinction is invisible for the comparison,
--
