research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-cauchy-product-of-convergent-series-diverges.md-1927-6.1 Translation to the root form: $G = \big(\prod_{k<n} a_k\big)^{1/n}$ satisfies $G \ge 0$ and $G^{n} = \prod_{k<n} a_k \le A^{n}$ with $A \ge 0$, so $G \le A$, since $G > A$ would give $G^{n} > A^{n}$; and $G = A$ holds exactly when $G^{n} = A^{n}$, by injectivity of $x \mapsto x^{n}$ on the nonnegatives, hence exactly when all $a_k$ are equal. [step 5.1, L2, L3, discharge-induction] ∎
